      "content": "those are actually pretty good. \"the snag\" or \"static\" feels much more accurate to the frustration we're feeling. \n\nbut i'm trying to find a way to bridge that into the actual review text. i want to explain that even if the lateness seems \"small\" or \"unimportant\" to them, it's essentially like a tiny, unseen force that's constantly messing with our efficiency. \n\ncan you try drafting a sentence or two using one of those \"nuisance\" metaphors? like, how do i say \"your lateness causes small, annoying disruptions to our workflow\" without sounding like i'm just complaining about the time? i want it to feel a bit more... descriptive of the actual effect on the system.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
